"""Alchemist, Valda's Spire of Secrets 2024 (Mage Hand Press). Own wording."""
CLASS = {
 "eq": ["2 Daggers, Leather Armor, Alchemist's Supplies, Alchemist's Fire, Scholar's Pack, 6 GP", "160 GP"],
 "f": {
  "Bombs": "You make unstable alchemical Bombs. You are proficient with them and can use the Explode mastery property with them. **Intelligent Explosions.** When you use Explode, you can add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to the damage roll. **Alchemist Save DC.** The DC for your Alchemist features, and for a Bomb in place of the Explode DC, is 8 + your Intelligence modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. **Bomb Supply.** Alchemist's Supplies let you make as many Bombs as you need for the day at no cost. To count them instead, you make 10 + twice your Alchemist level after each Short or Long Rest. Unused Bombs go inert after 24 hours.",
  "Potion Brewing": "Spend 10 minutes and expend Reagents to brew potions. You can do this during a Short Rest. The Potions table gives the Reagent cost and the Alchemist level each potion needs. You can hold a number of potions equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1). They stay potent until you finish a Long Rest. When you brew, you can also distill potions you already made. That destroys them and returns Reagents, up to the number in the Reagents column, and you can spend those Reagents right away. Drinking one of your potions while another is active has no unpredictable effect. **Potions by level.** Level 1: Climbing 1, Diminution 1, Growth 2, Healing 1, Resistance 1, Water Breathing 1. Level 4: Greater Healing 2, Invisibility 2, Sovereign Glue 1, Universal Solvent 1. Level 8: Heroism 3, Hill Giant Strength 3, Superior Healing 3. Level 12: Flying 5, Frost Giant Strength 4, Stone Giant Strength 4, Invulnerability 6. Level 16: Fire Giant Strength 7, Speed 9. The numbers are Reagents.",
  "Reagents": "You carry Reagents that fuel potions and other Alchemist features. You start with 2 and gain more as shown in the Reagents column. A Short Rest returns one expended Reagent. A Long Rest returns all of them.",
  "Prime Bomb": "Once per turn, when you hit with a Bomb or use Explode, you can expend 1 Reagent to add 1d10 to the Bomb damage. At higher levels you can expend more, up to the Prime Bomb column, and each Reagent adds 1d10. With Explode, each Reagent spent also lets you widen the blast radius by up to 5 feet. Example: at level 5, spending 2 Reagents adds 2d10 and lets the sphere be 5, 10, or 15 feet in radius.",
  "Bomb Formulas": "You learn formulas that change a Bomb just before you throw it. Choose three at level 2, and more at the levels in the Formulas column. After a Long Rest you can swap one formula for another. A formula granted by another feature does not count against your total. Once per turn, when you attack with a Bomb or use Explode, you can apply one formula to it. Some formulas change the damage dice and type. Improved Bombs damage applies from level 5. Formulas never change the size of Prime Bomb dice.",
  "Reagent Synthesis": "When you finish a Short Rest, you regain extra expended Reagents, up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1). Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Long Rest.",
  "Discovery": "Your research reveals secrets of alchemy. Choose one Discovery. You gain another at levels 9, 13, and 17. You cannot take the same Discovery twice. When you gain an Alchemist level, you can swap one Discovery for another you qualify for.",
  "Improved Bombs": "Once per turn, when you deal damage with a Bomb, its damage dice become 2d10. The dice grow again at the levels shown in the Bomb Damage column.",
  "Evasion": "When an effect lets you make a Dexterity save for half damage, you take no damage on a success and half on a failure. You lose this while Incapacitated.",
  "Blast Coating": "You automatically succeed on saves against your own Bombs and never take damage from them.",
  "Potion Mixologist": "As a Bonus Action, you can mix two potions and drink them together, gaining both effects. Mixing has no unexpected side effects for you.",
  "Experimentalist": "After a Long Rest, you can replace any of your Bomb Formulas, and you can replace one Discovery with another you qualify for.",
  "Nuclear Bomb": "You can convert a Bomb into the most destructive formula possible by loading your Philosopher's Stone as its core. You must use Explode. The Bomb deals 10d10 + 100 Force damage instead of Fire, in a sphere with a 1 mile radius. The blast destroys your Philosopher's Stone.",
  "Philosopher's Stone": "You craft the crowning work of alchemy, a glowing fist-sized jewel full of alchemical energy. If it is destroyed, you can build a new one with Alchemist's Supplies, materials worth at least 1,000 GP, and 7 days of work. You can have only one. While you have it: **Regenerating Reagents.** When you roll Initiative, you regain Reagents until you have 6, if you have 5 or fewer. **Quick Brewing.** You can brew potions as a Utilize action instead of taking 10 minutes. **Longevity.** You age one year for every ten that pass.",
 },
 "res": [{"n": "Reagents", "tag": "Short Rest 1, Long Rest all", "reset": "long", "max": "col:Reagents"}],
 "lu": [{"feature": "Reagent Synthesis", "n": "Reagent Synthesis", "lvl": 2, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Short Rest"}],
 "acts": {"Potion Brewing": "other", "Potion Mixologist": "bonus"},
 "opts": [{"feature": "Bomb Formulas", "title": "Bomb Formula", "types": ["BF"], "col": "Formulas"},
          {"feature": "Discovery", "title": "Discovery", "types": ["DO"], "levels": [5, 9, 13, 17]}],
 "opt": {"BF": {
   'Acid Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Acid damage instead of Fire and all its damage dice are d8s. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, has a -3 penalty to AC until the start of your next turn.',
   'Bramble Bomb': 'The Bomb deals no damage. With Explode, creatures make a Strength save instead of Dexterity. The blast area fills with thorny brambles and becomes Difficult Terrain. A target on the ground that is hit, or fails its save, is entangled: its Speed is 0 and cannot increase. An entangled creature can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your Alchemist save DC to break free. The brambles wither after 1 minute.',
   'Concussion Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Thunder damage instead of Fire. With Explode, creatures make a Constitution save instead of Dexterity. A Huge or smaller target hit by the Bomb is pushed 10 feet away from you. A Huge or smaller creature that fails its save against the explosion is pushed 10 feet away from the center of the blast.',
   'Cryo Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Cold damage instead of Fire and all its damage dice are d8s. With Explode, creatures make a Constitution save instead of Dexterity. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, has a -3 penalty to attack rolls until the start of your next turn.',
   'Fear Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Psychic damage instead of Fire and all its damage dice are d6s. With Explode, creatures make a Wisdom save instead of Dexterity. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn.',
   'Holy Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Radiant damage instead of Fire. Against a Fiend or Undead that takes damage from it, the Bomb damage dice become d12s.',
   'Impact Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Force damage instead of Fire and all its damage dice are d8s. With Explode, creatures make a Strength save instead of Dexterity. A Huge or smaller target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, has the Prone condition.',
   'Incendiary Bomb': 'All the Bomb damage dice are d8s. With Explode, the blast area burns until the start of your next turn. A creature that enters the area or ends its turn there must succeed on a Dexterity save or take Fire damage equal to the Bomb damage dice.',
   'Laughing Gas Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Poison damage instead of Fire and all its damage dice are d8s. With Explode, creatures make a Constitution save instead of Dexterity. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, laughs uncontrollably until the start of your next turn. It has the Poisoned condition and cannot cast spells with a Verbal component.',
   'Lightning Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Lightning damage instead of Fire. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn.',
   'Oil Bomb': 'The Bomb deals no damage. Instead the target, or each creature in the Explode sphere, is coated in flammable oil for 1 minute, or until it or another creature uses the Utilize action to wipe it off. The next time an oil-coated creature takes Fire damage, you can treat a roll of 1 to 3 on any damage die as a 4. This uses up the oil.',
   'Paint Bomb': 'The Bomb deals no damage. It splatters magical pigment across the Explode sphere. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, is coated in paint until the start of your next turn. A coated creature cannot benefit from the Invisible condition, and attacks against it have Advantage.',
   'Prismatic Bomb': 'The Bomb deals a random damage type instead of Fire, and Explode uses a random save type. Roll on both tables. Damage type (d6): 1 Acid, 2 Cold, 3 Fire, 4 Lightning, 5 Poison, 6 Radiant. Save type (d6): 1-2 Dexterity, 3-4 Constitution, 5-6 Wisdom.',
   'Quiet Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Bludgeoning damage instead of Fire. It detonates with only a soft thud, audible to 10 feet, and a puff of smoke hides the flash. When this Bomb reduces a creature to 0 Hit Points, you can knock it out instead: it drops to 1 Hit Point and stays Unconscious until it regains Hit Points or someone uses an action to give first aid (DC 10 Wisdom (Medicine) check).',
   'Seeking Bomb': 'Your ranged attack with this Bomb, and its explosion, ignore half and three-quarters cover.',
   'Smoke Bomb': "The Bomb deals no damage. It creates a sphere of smoke that is Heavily Obscured. The sphere's radius is twice the Explode radius. The smoke lasts 1 minute or until a strong wind, such as Gust of Wind, scatters it.", 'Teleportation Bomb': 'The Bomb deals no damage. Instead you teleport to the point where it lands. The teleport fails if the Bomb explodes more than 30 feet from you.',
   'Withering Bomb': 'The Bomb deals Necrotic damage instead of Fire and all its damage dice are d8s. With Explode, creatures make a Constitution save instead of Dexterity. A target hit by it, or that fails its save against it, has a -3 penalty to saving throws until the start of your next turn.'},
 "DO": {'Alchemy of Alteration': '**Batch Brewing.** You can hold 2 more potions at once. **Potion Ingredients.** You gain 4 extra Reagents that can only be spent on brewing potions. **Expanded Potions.** You can brew more potions, using your Alchemist save DC for any save they force. Level 5: Gaseous Form 2 Reagents, Philter of Love 1, Mind Reading 1, Animal Friendship 1. Level 8: Oil of Etherealness 3. Level 12: Oil of Slipperiness 5.', 'Alchemy of Poison': "**Batch Brewing.** You can hold 2 more potions at once. **Poisoner's Kit.** You gain proficiency with it. **Potent Poison.** Your Poison damage rolls ignore Resistance to Poison damage. **Poison Crafting.** You can brew these poisons from the 5th Edition rules, using your Alchemist save DC for any save they force. They count toward your potion limit. Level 5: Carrion Crawler Mucus 2 Reagents, Lolth's Sting 2, Serpent Venom 2. Level 8: Malice 3, Burnt Othur Fumes 3, Oil of Taggit 3. Level 12: Wyvern Poison 4.", 'Alchemy of Restoration': '**Batch Brewing.** You can hold 2 more potions at once. **Double Dose.** A Potion of Healing, Greater Healing, or Superior Healing you brew has two uses. Drinking it spends one use. **Expanded Potions.** Level 5: Elixir of Health 2 Reagents. Level 8: Potion of Longevity 4. Level 12: Potion of Vitality 4, Potion of Supreme Healing 6.', 'Arcane Studies': "**Two Cantrips.** You learn two Wizard cantrips. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for this Discovery. **Level 1 and 2 Spells.** Choose one level 1 and one level 2 Wizard spell. You always have them prepared. You can cast each once without a slot, and regain that use after a Long Rest. You can also restore a use with the Magic action by spending Reagents equal to the spell's level. You can cast them with spell slots too. **Spell Change.** When you gain a level, you can swap one of these spells for another of the same level from the Wizard list.", 'Combat Studies': '**Martial Training.** You gain proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor and Shields. **Breacher.** As a Bonus Action, you can attack with a weapon that is not a Bomb and lacks the Heavy property. **Fire Brand.** When you hit with a Melee weapon attack, you can spend 1 Reagent to deal an extra 1d10 Fire damage.', 'Fundamental Alchemy': "**Quadruple Flasks.** When you brew potions, you can spend 1 Reagent to make a batch of four vials of Acid, Alchemist's Fire, Holy Water, or Oil, in any mix. A batch counts as one potion toward your limit. These use your Alchemist save DC and stay potent until you finish a Long Rest. **Quick Flask.** When you take the Attack action with a Bomb, you can use a Bonus Action to throw a flask of Alchemist's Fire, Holy Water, Oil, or Acid, or to douse a space with an Oil flask. **Potent Flasks.** Brewed Acid, Alchemist's Fire, and Holy Water deal one extra die of damage. Alchemist's Fire also gives that die to burning creatures. Burning Oil adds your Intelligence modifier to its extra Fire damage.", 'Guided Explosives': '**Improved Bombs.** You get +1 to attack rolls with your Bomb. **Aerodynamic Bombs.** The normal and long ranges of your Bomb double. **Seeking Charge.** When you miss with a Bomb attack, you can spend 1 Reagent to roll 1d8 and add it to the attack roll, which may turn the miss into a hit.', 'Homunculus': '**Creating a Homunculus.** Spend 3 Reagents and materials worth 10 GP or more in a 1-hour process, which can happen during a Short Rest. You can have one at a time, and making another kills the first. **Hit Points.** It has Hit Points equal to five times your Alchemist level. **Bomb Immunity.** It automatically succeeds on saves against your Bombs and takes no damage from them. **Combat.** It is an ally to you and your allies. It acts right before or after your turn each round (your choice). It cannot attack on its own turn but can take other actions and Bonus Actions. As a Bonus Action, you can command it to attack with its Reaction. Its attack bonus equals your Intelligence modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. **Elemental Infusion.** As a Magic action, spend 2 Reagents to infuse it for 1 hour. Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. It gains Resistance to that damage and deals 2d8 extra damage of that type on its damage rolls.', 'Necrobiology': '**Hemoreagent.** As a Bonus Action, spend any number of Hit Point Dice to regain expended Reagents equal to half the dice spent (round down). **Lazarus Bolt.** As a Magic action, shock back to life a creature within 5 feet that died in the last minute. It returns with 1 Hit Point and gains Temporary Hit Points equal to twice your Alchemist level. It fails on creatures without a heart, that died of old age, or that lack vital organs. You can use it once per Long Rest, or restore the use by spending 3 Reagents (no action).', 'Precision Explosives': '**Improved Bombs.** You get +1 to your Alchemist save DC, rising to +2 at Alchemist level 11. **Sculpt Explosion.** When you use Explode, choose up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) of the creatures in the blast. They automatically succeed on their saves and take no damage.', 'Unconventional Explosives': "**Explosive Missile.** When you take the Attack action with a Bomb, you can use a Bonus Action to load it on a crossbow and fire it. It uses the crossbow's range and cannot use Explode. You can still apply a formula and prime it. **Fire Eater.** When you take the Attack action, you can use a Bonus Action to drink the Bomb contents and spit them in a 15-foot Cone, which acts as the Explode area. You can apply a formula and prime it, and each Reagent spent on priming extends the Cone by 5 feet.", 'Unconventional Potions': '**Potion Toss.** As a Bonus Action, you can hurl a potion at an ally within 30 feet. The ally gains its benefits as if it drank it. **Reactionary Gulp.** After a creature you can see damages you, you can use your Reaction to drink a potion. This works for a healing potion even if the damage dropped you to 0 Hit Points.'}},
}
